+    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(list(nerf.parameters()) + [nn.Parameter(code) for code in latent_codes], lr=1e-4)
+    vgg_model = VGG16(pretrained=True)
+    
+    for epoch in range(num_epochs):
+        for i, (img, pose, mask) in enumerate(zip(images, poses, gt_masks)):
+            # Sample rays for this image based on pose
+            ray_o, ray_d = sample_rays_from_pose(pose)
+            
+            # Render
+            rendered_color, T_tf = compute_volumetric_rendering(ray_o, ray_d, nerf, latent_codes[i], t_n=0.0, t_f=10.0)
+            
+            # Predict Binary Mask
+            rendered_mask = (T_tf >= 0.5).float()
+            
+            # Compute Loss
+            loss = compute_loss(rendered_color, img, rendered_mask, mask, vgg_model)
+            
+            # Backpropagate
+            optimizer.zero_grad()
+            loss.backward()
+            optimizer.step()
+            
+    return nerf, latent_codes
 ```
 
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Noisy GAN Sampling:** Generated images may be corrupted or have incorrect pose labels. Mitigated by filtering images with confidence $< 0.5$ and using drivable area constraints [S1].
-*   **Inductive Bias Neglect:** Naive isolated reconstruction fails to learn shared priors. Addressed by joint optimization (GLO) [S1].
-*   **Precision:** L1 loss is used for photometric error, which is robust to outliers compared to L2 [S1].
-*   **Boundaries:** Shadow maps are pre-computed and cast at the bottom of objects to handle lighting interactions [S1].
